                <pb facs="0439" n="359" xml:id="pg359"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilson to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson reports, in connection with his dispatch of February 8, that a new
                    law has been passed by the Diet recognizing perpetual leases real rights,
                    applying to them code provisions relating to ownership. Provision is made for
                    unequivocal registration of leases free of charges, and for all rights of which
                    lease is the object. The exemption of houses in any way is not indicated.)</p>
            </div>
